  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back everywhere, so `OrderPlaced` carries it again. I haven't run CI or any npm script, because the sandbox denied shell commands that need approval.\n\nThe failure shows that `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). My earlier premise that nothing reads the field was wrong. The ARCH-4 contract check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't see it before removing the field.\n\nI restored the model, the event, the request parsing and validation, the tests, and the `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` examples. I did it by hand-editing instead of `git checkout`, which was also denied. A grep shows the same 17 `channel` occurrences across the `src` and `test` `.ts` files as before my change. Please run `git diff` to confirm nothing is left over, then run `npm test` and `npm run arch`. The `billing-service` check passed either way.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. Its owners would need to relax that contract, or we could bump `OrderPlaced` to `schemaVersion: 4` with the field removed and coordinate the cutover. Tell me which route you want and I'll make the change.",
